.Dd August 19, 2026
.Dt CODA-H "" "Coda-C"
.Os Multiplatform
.Sh NAME
.Nm coda-h
.Nd Header Generator (Version 6.1)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op option ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is used to generate headers for coda-c source files (*.c) in a single working folder.
The following files may be created: \fIcoda_generated.H\fR, \fIcoda_private.H\fR, \fIcoda_generated.c\fR.
The program can generate function prototypes, class and signature definitions,
prototypes for macro defined functions, and passthru header definitions, etc.
.sp
.Nm
without any arguments will generate headers if the file "coda.h" exists.
.Bl -tag -width "helpxx"
.It Fl h
Show usage information.
.It Fl f
force header generation without a "coda.h" file
.It Fl n
create a "coda.h" file and generate headers
.It Fl v
report additional information while processing
.It Fl q
report less information while processing
.It Fl l
check headers lines for white at end of lines (*.h)
.El
.Pp
.sp
If the keyword \fI"PRIVATE"\fR also appears on a line used to generate definitions, then these definitions
will be directed to the file \fIcoda_private.H\fR.
.sp
Lines starting with the C inline comment and a pipe symbol \fI"//|"\fR have these three characters
removed and are recorded in a header file.
.sp
Lines starting with the C inline comment and a greater than symbol \fI"//>"\fR symbol operate as above
except these lines are processed first and wind up at the top of the header.
.sp
For regular C function to be prototyped they must start at the start of line without proceeding white space.
.sp
Macros like \fICodaStatic()\fR (used to embed files) and \fICodaLink()\fR (used to force linkage)
will generate additional C code.
.sp
